xnu 0477: map the wifi pins beside the worker, not at the top of the block

Measured 2026-11-26: `0475` and `0476` both stop the boot probe block at the
eUSB2 map -- no `MONDR USB: eUSB2` line and no `probe done`, while `0474` prints
all three eUSB2 lines and `probe done`. The only change shared by the two bad
boots is `wifi_map_pins()` at the top of `mondrian_wifi_premap()`; `0474` did
not map the pin pages at boot at all.

The pin pages are now mapped by `mondrian_wifi_premap_pins()` right before
`mondrian_wifi_start()` inside `mondrian_usb_probe()`, which is also where the
worker starts again (the `0474` placement that reached `W4 identity`). The
worker still takes no `ml_io_map()` of its own, and the eUSB2 block runs in the
same conditions as `0474`. `eUSB2 map start` and `eUSB2 done` name the block if
it stops again.
